{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"balladic-fattening-tortoise","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nOn the operator's macOS host, the system temp dir (`tempfile.gettempdir()`, /var/folders/.../T) holds 575 `rebar-opcert-*` directories, each with an `opcert-key` file that begins `-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----` (256 also hold `opcert-key.pub`). Modification dates: 144 on 2026-10-28, 135 on 10-29, 144 on 10-30, 153 on 10-31 (measured 2026-10-31).\n\n`rebar.opcert_service.keyprov.compose_signer` creates exactly this shape (`tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rebar-opcert-\")` + `opcert-key` copy) and only `OpcertSigner.cleanup()` removes it.\n\n## Unverified (next checks)\nWhich caller leaks them is not established. Callers that construct a signer: 6 unit-test modules (test_opcert_service*.py, test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py, test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py, test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py) and `mcp_server.compose_startup_opcert_binding`. Next check: run each of those modules alone and count new `rebar-opcert-*` dirs before and after.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaking caller(s) identified by a before/after count.\n- [ ] Running the unit suite leaves no new `rebar-opcert-*` directory in the system temp dir (regression test).\n- [ ] Existing leaked copies are removed by the operator (not by tooling) after the fix lands.","id":"89d1-eb1f-aa57-49a6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["security","opcert","tests"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Signer key copies leak into the host temp dir (~140 rebar-opcert-* private keys per day)"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793506206011741001,"uuid":"ad033496-7a25-49d7-a9b1-d75e3005fefd"}